# rena0-air-turn — F1-3 fixture, P2-7 air family (the airborne turn)
#
# Source: the airborne movement branch (FUN_00428510 @0x428d9b) writes +0x874 =
# 0x40000000 (2.0 degrees/tick) and calls FUN_00421780, which turns the body yaw toward
# the input's compass bearing by at most that step (FUN_0042db10's bounded turn). Holding
# a direction mid-air therefore rotates the character, at 2 degrees per tick — the ground
# turn's airborne counterpart.
#
# The port had no airborne turn at all: its turn block only runs in the Walk state, so a
# jump followed by Left/Right moved without rotating. `turn_deg` is the per-tick facing
# delta, so -2/+2 is the recovered rate, not the accumulated angle.
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 2000
collision open-field
# An input line REPLACES the held mask, so JUMP is repeated on the direction lines to
# keep the whole case airborne (the climb lasts until the meter empties).
input 0 JUMP
input 20 LEFT JUMP
expect 22 turn_deg -2
expect 26 turn_deg -2
expect 32 turn_deg -2
input 60 RIGHT JUMP
expect 62 turn_deg 2
expect 70 turn_deg 2
